  "description": "NARXIQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H96 Er4 N12 O16,C2 H3 N1,0.5(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.503-3.801 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.18-111.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C118.5H99ClEr4N13O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
